   "text": {
    "L1": "Rounding gives an estimate: a nearby number that is easier to use. We can round to the nearest 10, 100 or 1000.",
    "L2": "First find the two neighbours: the place values just below and just above the number.",
    "L3": "Then find the halfway mark between those neighbours. Below halfway goes down; halfway and above goes up.",
    "L4": "For 7380, the thousand neighbours are 7000 and 8000. The halfway mark is 7500.",
    "L5": "7380 is less than 7500, so it rounds to 7000. We decide in one step from the original number.",
    "L6": "To round to the nearest thousand, look at the hundreds digit. To round to the nearest hundred, look at the tens digit.",
    "L7": "MYTH: round in steps, like 1450 to 1500 and then 2000. NOT TRUE: rounding an already-rounded number can give the wrong answer.",
    "L8": "Now use the same halfway idea. Which thousand is 7380 nearer to?"
   },
